course: dictionary
lesson: 13740
title: Inter: burial, between, and a name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «inter» has three different jobs. In formal writing, to inter means to bury a dead person in a grave or tomb. «The soldier was interred in the churchyard.» The words churchyard and grave are the clues, so interred means buried.
explain: At the start of a word, inter- often means between or among. «The international match was played between two countries.» Here international means between nations, because nation is the word after inter-. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about things between or among others?
explain: A capital I can be a name. «Inter scored twice in the match» is about a football team, not burial or the prefix. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Inter (verb) means to bury a dead person in a grave or tomb.
fact: «Interred» is the past form, and «interring» is the -ing form.
fact: The prefix «inter-» means between or among.
fact: Words with inter-: international (between nations), interact (act between people), interval (a gap between things), internet (a network between computers).
fact: «Inter» is also the short name of Inter Milan, an Italian football club.
exercise: «The soldier was interred in the churchyard.» What does interred mean? | Thrown into the river | Painted in bright colours | *Buried in a grave | Lost on the way home
exercise: Which word means between two countries? | *international | internal | national | interior
exercise: Ali says, «Inter scored twice in the match.» What is Inter in this sentence? | A type of rain | A country in Europe | A kind of church | *An Italian football club
test: «The family interred their old dog under the apple tree.» What does interred mean here? | *Buried in the ground | Hidden under a bed | Washed clean | Planted as a tree
test: In «interact», what does the prefix inter- mean? | Above | *Between or among | Without | Under
exam: Which word uses the prefix inter- to mean between or among? | *interact | repaint | unhappy | football
